cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spectrl, please cite this software using these metadata."
title: "spectrl: URL-safe interchange for mass spectra"
abstract: >-
  spectrl encodes a mass spectrum — peak arrays, modeled metadata, and precursor
  information — into a single compact, URL-safe token, enabling spectra to be
  shared directly in URLs, QR codes, notebooks, and publications without a
  backend repository. Metadata uses established mzML controlled-vocabulary
  semantics and may include a ProForma interpretation.
type: software
